# Prime source-to-licensed-execution theory crown

This is the intentional import gate for the current Prime theory tranche.  A
successful build checks one connected dependency graph containing:

* compile-time MeTTa expression and complete-program quotation;
* proof-carrying raw, eager, and suspended program-island preparation;
* the dependent rho interaction fibre and its non-collapse boundary;
* finite-family separation, occurrence-indexed conflict colourings, and
  work/span schedules;
* generic typed optimization admission with independent semantic and
  profitability evidence;
* the program-level gradual guarantee derived from the native seam; and
* source-occurrence adequacy from authored programs through Prime interaction
  terms to ordinary authorized GSLT paths.

The gate does not claim a CeTTa implementation of these interfaces.  It
collects the reference semantics and theorems that such an implementation
must refine.
